   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5f30757a-c5a4-4179-bd03-f95f5d984ee3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Key Findings\n",
    "1. Total sales of 2.06M generated profit of 259K (margin 12.6%).\n",
    "2. Supplies, Bookcases, and Tables are loss-making sub-categories.\n",
    "3. Orders with no discount earn a 29.8% margin, and orders with 1-20% discounts stay profitable at 12.2%. Orders with 21-40% discounts have a margin of -15.6%, and those above 40% have -76%.\n",
    "4. The Central region has the lowest margin. The least profitable states are Texas (Central) and Ohio (East).\n",
    "5. Sales peak in November and December each year.\n",
    "6. Note: about 10% of rows with missing or invalid Sales/Profit values were excluded from the analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Recommendations\n",
    "1. Cap discounts at 20% for loss-making sub-categories, and require approval above that level.\n",
    "2. Review pricing and supplier costs for Tables, Bookcases, and Supplies.\n",
    "3. Investigate whether heavy discounting explains the losses in Texas and Ohio, and set stricter discount limits there if it does.\n",
    "4. Prepare inventory and marketing for the November-December peak."
   ]
  },
